    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 1+2: a `.feature` file absent from the commit tree is graceful.\n\n    The slice commit DELETES `removed.feature` -- `git show --name-only` lists\n    it as touched, so the P4 existence probe iterates it and probes\n    `git show {commit}:removed.feature`, which resolves nothing in the commit\n    tree. The probe must treat that absent path as not-in-commit -- skip it,\n    continue -- never raise `CalledProcessError`.\n\n    The commit carries no genuine `@slice-01` `.feature` AT in its tree, so\n    P4 legitimately REFUSES (`SliceReverifyRefused`, exit 1) -- reaching a\n    clean precondition verdict instead of crashing with a traceback.\n    ": 0.15231472899904475,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 1: a commit equal to HEAD -> `SliceReverifyRefused`, exit 1.\n\n    The slice commit IS HEAD -- no commit buries it. P5 refuses with exit 1\n    BEFORE any gate runs (preconditions run before gates), so the refusal\n    appends NO ledger record. This is the reverify-as-bypass-vector closure:\n    a still-HEAD slice belongs to the U2 G_COMMIT exit gate.\n    ": 0.12415135797346011,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 1: reverify of `slice-02` with an unverified `slice-01` refused.\n\n    The ledger carries no `SliceCommitVerified` record for `slice-01`. P6\n    refuses with exit 1 BEFORE any gate runs, and the refusal appends NO\n    ledger record. This closes the out-of-order-mint hole: reverify cannot\n    mint a `slice-02` record while `slice-01` is M8-invisible.\n    ": 0.16798115900019184,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 2: `--commit HEAD` (zero commits buried) -> refused, exit 1.\n\n    Passing the literal ref `HEAD` resolves to the slice commit itself --\n    `git rev-list HEAD..HEAD` is empty, zero commits bury it. P5 refuses\n    regardless of whether the commit-ish is a SHA or the symbolic `HEAD`.\n    ": 0.1331665050238371,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 2: an AT deleted post-commit emits `SliceReverifyRefused`.\n\n    The slice's `@slice-01` `.feature` once lived in the slice commit but was\n    later removed from the tree. E1 (working-tree walk) would now pass\n    vacuously -- P4, reading the commit tree, refuses with exit 1 and appends\n    NO ledger record (preconditions run before any gate).\n    ": 0.657013199001085,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 2: reverify of `slice-01` passes P6 vacuously.\n\n    `slice-01` has no predecessor -- P6 is the base case and never refuses.\n    The `orphaned_green_slice_repo` reverify of `slice-01` proceeds past the\n    precondition group to a `SliceReverified` success.\n    ": 15.88834218296688,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 2: zero in-commit ATs -> `SliceReverifyRefused`, exit 1.\n\n    The slice commit carries the trailer (P2 passes) and is an ancestor of\n    HEAD (P1 passes) but no `@slice-01` `.feature` file at all. P4 refuses\n    with exit 1 BEFORE any gate runs, and the refusal appends NO ledger\n    record.\n    ": 0.637606285919901,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 3: a commit carrying its `.feature` AT passes P4.\n\n    The `orphaned_green_slice_repo` slice commit ships its `@slice-01`\n    `.feature` file. P4 finds it in the commit tree, the precondition group\n    passes, and reverify proceeds to a `SliceReverified` success.\n    ": 22.02933166496223,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 3: a genuinely-buried slice commit passes P5.\n\n    In `orphaned_green_slice_repo` a later commit grows the contract suite\n    AFTER the slice commit -- so the slice commit is a STRICT ancestor of\n    HEAD with one commit between it and HEAD. P5 passes, the precondition\n    group passes, and reverify proceeds to a `SliceReverified` success.\n    ": 17.03091459296411,
    "tests/des/acceptance/test_reverify_slice_commit.py::::Criterion 3: a successful reverify appends a `SliceReverified` record.\n\n    The success path appends TWO adjacent HMAC-chained ledger records: the\n    `SliceCommitVerified` record (M8-visible) and a `SliceReverified`\n    provenance record (I-6). `verified_slices()` keys only on\n    `SliceCommitVerified`, so its shape is unchanged -- the provenance\n    record makes the recovery path auditable without altering ordering.\n    ": 16.342539598990697,
